{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795776209,"nonce":"/hSg5StosE05l4mzhlzLP1x8NA0=","title":"A frame with glass loses background images and image placeholders","message":"On a page with a glass element anywhere:\n\n- Through the window compositor, no background image shows when the page has an opaque background. frame_dispatch drew the images into the target first, then render_glass_frame painted the background primitives over them, and only the layer-effects branch drew the images again.\n- The glass did not blur an image under it, because the backdrop also had the images under the background.\n- No image placeholder of any kind is drawn. render_images_ref skipped unloaded images. It is also the draw path of the compositor's cached replays.\n- render_images_ref passed a scale factor of 1 to the image instance, so a CSS translate on an image was not scaled on a HiDPI display.\n- A frame drawn in separate steps (layer effects, overlay) called render_glass, which does not draw nested_glass_primitives.\n\nFound while fixing 3b63ceb, which needs a glass frame to keep the other images.","files":null}]}